---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { GA4_ID } from '../data/site-config';
---

<BaseLayout noAds title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy Policy for Resurgence Builds: how we handle your data, cookies, and third-party advertising." breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy Policy', url: '/privacy/' }]}>
  <div class="container section content-width">
    <h1 class="heading-accent">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p style="color:var(--ink-muted);">Last updated: October 31, 2026</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Introduction</h2>
      <p>Resurgence Builds ("we," "our," or "us") operates the website resurgencebuilds.com. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your information when you visit our site.</p>

      <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>We don't require user accounts. The only information we collect ourselves is what you choose to post in a comment and the tier you pick when you vote (see <a href="#comments">Comments</a> and <a href="#votes">Votes</a> below). Third-party services integrated into our site may collect certain information automatically, including:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>IP address and general location data (via {GA4_ID ? 'Cloudflare, Google AdSense and Google Analytics' : 'Cloudflare and Google AdSense'})</li>
        <li>Browser type, device type, and operating system</li>
        <li>Pages visited and time spent on the site</li>
        <li>Advertising interaction data (via Google AdSense)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Third-Party Advertising</h2>
      <p>We use <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Google AdSense</strong></a> to display advertisements on our site. Google AdSense uses cookies and similar technologies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website and other websites. This includes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Placing tracking cookies on your device to personalize advertisements</li>
        <li>Using the DoubleClick cookie to enable interest-based advertising</li>
        <li>Collecting data about your browsing behavior across websites that use Google advertising services</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Ads Settings</a>. You may also opt out of third-party vendor cookies by visiting the <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Network Advertising Initiative opt-out page</a>.</p>
      <p>For more information about how Google uses data when you use our site, visit <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's partner sites policy</a>.</p>

      {GA4_ID && (
        <>
          <h2>Analytics</h2>
          <p>We use <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Google Analytics</strong></a> to count visits and see which pages are read, so we know what to update. It sets cookies that record pages viewed, time on the site, device type and approximate location. We don't send Google your name or email. You can opt out with <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's opt-out browser add-on</a>.</p>
        </>
      )}

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>Our site uses cookies from the following categories:</p>
      <h3>Essential Cookies</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare:</strong> Security and performance cookies required for content delivery, DDoS protection, and edge routing. These are necessary for the site to function properly.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Functional Cookies</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>rb_voter:</strong> set only when you rank a build or OS Protocol, so your next pick changes your vote instead of adding another. It's a random code, sent only to our vote counter, and lasts up to 400 days. See <a href="#votes">Votes</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Advertising Cookies</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google AdSense:</strong> Tracking cookies used to serve personalized advertisements based on your browsing history. These cookies may track your activity across multiple websites. You can manage your ad personalization preferences at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      {GA4_ID && (
        <>
          <h3>Analytics Cookies</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Google Analytics:</strong> Cookies that tell one visit from another and group page views into sessions, so we can count readers and see which pages they use. You can opt out with <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's opt-out browser add-on</a>.</li>
          </ul>
        </>
      )}

      <h2 id="comments">Comments</h2>
      <p>Articles, builds and guides have an open comment section: type a name and a comment, no account needed. Here's what that involves.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>What's public:</strong> the name you type, your comment and the date. Use a nickname if you like; don't post personal details.</li>
        <li><strong>What we store privately:</strong> the page, the time, and a scrambled code made from your IP address (a salted hash), used only to stop spam and limit how fast one person can post. We never store or show the IP address itself.</li>
        <li><strong>In your browser:</strong> the name you used is remembered in your browser's local storage so you don't have to type it again. It isn't a cookie and isn't sent anywhere until you post.</li>
        <li><strong>Moderation:</strong> an automatic filter (Cloudflare Workers AI) checks each comment as it's posted, and we review new and reported comments twice a day. Removed comments are deleted for good within 30 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Removal requests:</strong> email <a href="mailto:p1@cfworx.tech">p1@cfworx.tech</a> with the page and the name you used, and we'll delete your comment.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Comment rules</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Keep it about the game, the build or the article. Disagree all you want; attack ideas, not people.</li>
        <li>No hate speech, harassment, threats, sexual content or personal information about anyone.</li>
        <li>No spam, ads, links or email addresses (links are blocked automatically), and no pretending to be the site, Ubisoft or someone else.</li>
        <li>No cheats, exploits for sale, account selling or anything that breaks Ubisoft's terms.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We remove comments that break these rules and block repeat offenders. You can flag a comment with its Report button: we look at every report, and a comment that several people report is hidden until we do.</p>

      <h2 id="votes">Votes</h2>
      <p>Both tier lists are ranked by readers: you can rank any build or OS Protocol S to D, no account needed. Here's what that involves.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>What's public:</strong> only the totals (how many S, A, B, C and D votes each item has). Nobody can see who voted what.</li>
        <li><strong>What we store privately:</strong> the item, your pick, the time, the random code from the rb_voter cookie, and scrambled codes made from your network's IP address and your browser's user agent (salted hashes). They keep it to one vote per person and stop vote spam. We never store the IP address itself.</li>
        <li><strong>In your browser:</strong> your picks are remembered in local storage so the page can highlight them. That isn't sent anywhere.</li>
        <li><strong>Removal requests:</strong> email <a href="mailto:p1@cfworx.tech">p1@cfworx.tech</a> with what you ranked and roughly when, and we'll find and delete those votes.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare:</strong> Hosting, CDN, security, comment and vote storage, and comment filtering (Cloudflare D1 and Workers AI)</li>
        <li><strong>Google AdSense:</strong> Advertising (<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>)</li>
        {GA4_ID && <li><strong>Google Analytics:</strong> Visit counts and page reports (<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>)</li>}
        <li><strong>Google Fonts:</strong> Typography</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>GDPR Rights (EU Users)</h2>
      <p>Under GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access your personal data</li>
        <li>Rectify inaccurate data</li>
        <li>Erase your data ("right to be forgotten")</li>
        <li>Restrict processing</li>
        <li>Data portability</li>
        <li>Object to processing, including profiling for advertising purposes</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Please note that advertising data collected by Google AdSense is processed by Google under their own privacy policy. To exercise your rights regarding Google's data collection, visit <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>. For data we control, contact us at <a href="mailto:p1@cfworx.tech">p1@cfworx.tech</a>.</p>

      <h2>CalOPPA Compliance (California Users)</h2>
      <p>We do not sell personal information. Third-party advertising partners (Google AdSense) may collect data for interest-based advertising as described above. We honor Do Not Track browser signals where technically feasible. California residents may request details about data we hold by contacting us.</p>

      <h2>Data Security</h2>
      <p>We serve all content over HTTPS with HSTS enabled. We do not store passwords, payment information, or sensitive personal data. Comments and votes are stored in Cloudflare's database with IP addresses reduced to a salted hash. Advertising data is processed by Google under their own security standards.</p>

      <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>Our site is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect data from children. Google AdSense is configured to comply with COPPA requirements.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy. Changes will be posted here with an updated date.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Email <a href="mailto:p1@cfworx.tech">p1@cfworx.tech</a>.</p>
      <p>Publisher mailing address available upon written request to <a href="mailto:p1@cfworx.tech">p1@cfworx.tech</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
